{
	"$comment": "Merch print files only (no mockups). Item list, trim sizes, bleed and safe areas are common vendor print areas (the spyglass-ds and context-ds engines use the same conventions; confirm with the vendor template). Layouts are in inches from the trim. Only the approved lockups (logo.json: the octopus and wordmark, the wordmark alone, the octopus alone) and the brand's own patterns (the wordmark tile, the outline band, hatching, the reef) are used. The octopus is full-color art, so it prints only on full-color variants; one-color variants (embroidery, one-ink screen print) carry the wordmark alone. Colors come from the variant, as tokens. Only the words that are passed are printed (sample copy with --sample). Highlighted words are pink on purple and ink, and rose (the pink's dark partner, 5.9:1 on white) elsewhere. A band or a tile prints whole wordmarks only, inside the safe area; the reef, the hatching and a printed ground run into the bleed. Business cards, letterheads, a report cover, a certificate, an event badge, a name tag and a notebook cover are derived the same way (the brand made none of its own): see each item's source.",
